# Cline Rules for Omega Document Creator

These rules exist to stop repeated false starts, false completion claims, stale docs, partial test runs, and Windows shell mistakes.

## 1. Environment

- Shell is PowerShell on Windows.
- Do not write bash-style command chains.
- Do not use `cmd.exe` syntax unless explicitly required.
- Prefer direct PowerShell commands and repo-local scripts.

Wrong:
- `cd apps/api && python -m pytest`
- `set VAR=value & python app.py`
- `pytest --timeout=60`

Correct:
- `Push-Location apps\api; .venv\Scripts\python -m pytest tests -v`
- `$env:VAR="value"; .venv\Scripts\python app.py`
- `python -m pytest tests -v`

## 2. Required Read Order At Start Of Every New Stage

Before making claims or edits, read these first:

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `.agent-handoff/codex-task.md`
3. `.agent-handoff/cline-result.md`
4. `.agent-handoff/validation-log.md`
5. `phases.md`
6. `PROJECT.md`
7. `.ai-codex/index.md`

Then read only the relevant `.ai-codex` scope files for the stage.

Do not skip this.

## 3. No False Completion Claims

Do not say a stage is complete unless all of these are true:

- code changes are actually present in the repo
- runtime wiring is actually connected, not just helper functions added
- verification commands were actually run
- docs match the current code
- the handoff files match the current code and test results

If something was only structurally reviewed but not executed, say so explicitly.

Never claim:
- "complete"
- "all tests pass"
- "verified"
- "no regressions"

unless you actually ran the relevant commands and checked the output.

## 4. Verification Is Mandatory

For Omega, verification is not optional.

### Backend

Always prefer the full backend suite, not a single test file, unless the prompt explicitly says to narrow scope.

Use:
- `$env:PYTHONPATH="apps\api"; apps\api\.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest apps/api/tests -v`

Do not use this as your only backend check unless explicitly told to:
- `apps/api/tests/test_api.py`

### Frontend

Always run both:
- `Push-Location apps\frontend; node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd --noEmit --project tsconfig.app.json`
- `Push-Location apps\frontend; node_modules\.bin\vitest.cmd run --no-cache`

Use `--no-cache` for Vitest in this repo because Google Drive/Windows cache behavior can be flaky.

### One-command validation

If `scripts/validate.ps1` exists, prefer it for full validation:
- `.\scripts\validate.ps1`

But still inspect what it actually runs before claiming broad coverage.

## 5. Full Test Scope Discipline

Do not quietly narrow test scope.

If CI or validation runs only part of the backend suite, say exactly that.

Bad:
- "backend pytest passes" when only `test_api.py` was run

Good:
- "backend API suite passes" if only `test_api.py` was run
- "full backend suite passes" only if `apps/api/tests` was run

## 6. Documentation Must Match Live Code

This repo has repeatedly drifted between docs and implementation.

Before marking a stage complete, check:

- `.agent-handoff/cline-result.md`
- `.agent-handoff/validation-log.md`
- `phases.md`
- `PROJECT.md`
- relevant `.ai-codex/*` files

against the actual code that changed.

If frontend behavior uses `localStorage`, docs must say so.
If Vitest now passes, remove claims about pre-existing failures.
If a route is live, do not leave docs saying it is missing.

## 7. Runtime Wiring Must Be Checked

Do not stop at "helper exists".

Examples of required checks:

- if `_csrf_check()` exists, verify it is called by middleware
- if rate limiting helper exists, verify login route actually calls it
- if lifespan/startup helper exists, verify app actually uses it
- if delete/download APIs exist, verify frontend uses them where claimed
- if a scheduler exists, verify startup and shutdown are wired

## 8. Frontend Rules For This Repo

- `income-protection-page.tsx` is fragile and large; make surgical changes only
- preserve existing route/UI behavior unless explicitly changing it
- do not remove `localStorage` behavior unless the stage explicitly requires it
- when fixing tests, prefer restoring honest existing behavior over rewriting large test surfaces

If you change frontend state behavior, re-check:
- `client-data-context.tsx`
- `App.tsx`
- `income-protection-page.tsx`
- `app.test.tsx`

## 9. Handoff File Discipline

If you touched a file, list it in `.agent-handoff/cline-result.md`.

If you ran verification, record:
- exact command
- exact result
- exact scope

in `.agent-handoff/validation-log.md`.

Do not leave stale counts like:
- old Vitest totals
- old pytest totals
- old failure descriptions

## 10. Local Artifact And Git Rules

Do not commit local/generated artifacts unless explicitly requested.

Usually exclude:
- `apps/vitest-app.txt`
- ad hoc scratch files
- editor-only local files
- logs

If `.clinerules` or another local control file is changed intentionally, include it only if requested.

Before commit/push:
- check `git status --short`
- confirm staged scope
- do not sweep unrelated changes into the commit

## 11. Current Known Good Commands

### Full backend tests
- `$env:PYTHONPATH="apps\api"; apps\api\.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest apps/api/tests -v`

### Frontend typecheck
- `Push-Location apps\frontend; node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd --noEmit --project tsconfig.app.json`

### Frontend tests
- `Push-Location apps\frontend; node_modules\.bin\vitest.cmd run --no-cache`

### Full validation
- `.\scripts\validate.ps1`

## 12. PowerShell Piping Warning — Chat Input Breaks With 2>&1

When running long CLI commands with `2>&1` (stderr-to-stdout redirect) at the end of a PowerShell command, Cline sometimes fails to capture streaming output properly. This causes the terminal response to hang and eventually time out — even though the command ran successfully.

**Rule:** Avoid appending `2>&1` to PowerShell test/build commands in this repo. Run them as:

```
Push-Location apps\frontend; node_modules\.bin\vitest.cmd run --no-cache -- src/app.test.tsx
```

Not:
```
Push-Location apps\frontend; node_modules\.bin\vitest.cmd run --no-cache -- src/app.test.tsx 2>&1
```

This also applies to `tsc` and `pytest` commands. The `2>&1` redirect appears to interfere with Cline's output streaming protocol on Windows.

## 13. Response Quality Rules

When reporting back:

- separate what was changed from what was only reviewed
- do not compress uncertainty into confident wording
- if something remains open, say it plainly
- if the stage is not clean, produce a fix-pass result instead of pretending it is done

This repo prefers strict truth over optimistic summaries.
